Implement user story SKY-002-b: Vitest tests for SkyscannerClient

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock the global fetch — no real network calls. Tests cover URL/header construction, successful parsing, HTTP errors, missing API key, malformed responses, and mock mode behavior.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked global fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach fetch restoration; tsc --noEmit and vitest run both exit 0 with no errors
- Test verifies searchFlights constructs the correct RapidAPI URL and sets the required headers (including the API key)
- Test verifies a successful API response is correctly parsed into a FlightResult[] matching the interface shape
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx responses cause searchFlights to reject with an Error containing the status code and NOT containing the apiKey value
- Test verifies constructing SkyscannerClient without an apiKey (or with empty string) when RAPIDAPI_KEY is unset/empty throws the missing-key Error
- Test verifies a malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with a descriptive parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' causes searchFlights to return deterministic fixture data without invoking fetch (spy/assert never called)
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API with non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') results in a real fetch call; real failures are never silently replaced with mock data


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class is exported from src/skyscanner/client.ts
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string })
- Constructor throws Error with message 'apiKey is required and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is not set' when resolvedKey is empty
- Constructor resolves apiKey in order: apiKey param (trimmed) -> process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY (trimmed) -> empty string
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- When process.env.MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API === 'true', searchFlights returns mock data without calling fetch
- Mock data is from #getMockFlights() which returns 3 FlightResult objects with deterministic values
- Mock flight data includes: MockAir (299 USD), TestJet (450 USD), BudgetFly (189 USD)
- For non-mock path, fetch is called with URL https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/search
- Query params set on URL: 'origin', 'destination', 'date', and optionally 'adults' if defined
- Fetch headers include: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with apiKey value, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP error handling: throws Error with message 'HTTP error: ${response.status}' when !response.ok
- JSON parse error handling: throws Error with message 'Invalid API response: malformed JSON' when response.json() fails
- #parseFlightResults validates response has 'itineraries' array property
- Parse error for missing itineraries: 'Invalid API response: missing or invalid itineraries array'
- Parse error when no valid results: 'Invalid API response: no valid flight results found'
- Parse error for non-object response: 'Invalid API response: expected object'
- Parsing extracts: price.amount, price.currency, legs[0].departure, legs[0].arrival, legs[0].duration, legs[0].stopCount or legs[0].stops, carriers[0].name or carriers[0].code
- Invalid itinerary entries are skipped (continue in loop) rather than causing hard failures
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API only matches exact string 'true' - other values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') result in real fetch call
- Error messages from HTTP responses contain status code but never contain the apiKey value

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
  })),
}));
```

